 "rule_variants": "Activation variants rule (addendum to rule.txt), written 2026-10-31T13:18:02+07:00 before any result of the variant runs exists. Not from a source. Not reviewed by the user. Scope: user approval of 2026-10-31 (\"l\u00e0m \u0111\u1ea7y \u0111\u1ee7 c\u00e1c bi\u1ebfn th\u1ec3 lu\u00f4n\"), advisor-reviewed design in tmp/2026-10-31_phase2b-variants-design.md. The 1.0 pp, 5 percent and 50 percent thresholds are the approved ones of gate G4 and are not changed.\nCandidates (seed 0 each, INT8 conclusion dtype, 1 seed): V1 LeakyReLU with negative slope 0.1 (ai/models/yolov8n_leakyrelu/yolov8n_leakyrelu.yaml, 100 epochs). The slope is one project choice, a convention of Darknet YOLO configs, not taken from T1 or T2 (the T1 entry has no slope constraint) and there is no sweep. V2 ReLU6 (yolov8n_relu6.yaml, 100 epochs). V3 ReLU 200 epochs (yolov8n_relu.yaml, config ppe5_yolov8n_relu_200ep.yaml). Control: SiLU baseline 200 epochs seed 0 (ppe5_yolov8n_baseline_200ep_s0), descriptive. All initialised from yolov8n.pt, trained with the same Ultralytics settings as the baseline (only the model yaml and the number of epochs differ), exported with the calibration list of baseline seed 0 (export_npu.py --calib-from) and evaluated as in rule.txt.\nPre-check (not a verdict): an FP16 RKNN build of the untrained yaml (nc 80) shows the fused op names before training: V1 51 ConvLeakyRelu and 6 ConvLeakyReluAdd, V2 57 ConvClip and 8 separate Add rows, CPU rows only InputOperator, Transpose, OutputOperator. The verdict of G3 comes from the trained INT8 build.\nGate G1 mapping rule (fixed now, the same as for ReLU): a fused name maps to the Operator List entry ConvolutionXxx by name. A fused name with an Add (ConvLeakyReluAdd, ConvReluAdd) has no entry of that name, so G1 is partial and the best possible label is 'Ch\u01b0a bi\u1ebft' even when A, B and C pass. V2 has no fused Add (pre-check), so its G1 can pass if the trained build confirms it.\nStatements, css_test, per candidate:\nV-C gate C: difference candidate minus SiLU seed 0 (100 epochs, the approved deployable baseline) in pp for AP50-95, AP NoHelmet, AP Vest at INT8. C passes only when all three differences are at least minus 1.0. FP16 is a reference, FP32 descriptive.\nV-E for V3 only: the same differences against the SiLU 200 epoch control, as description next to V-C. If V3 passes V-C the wording is 'ReLU 200 epoch \u0111\u1ea1t', never '\u0111\u1ed5i activation \u0111\u1ea1t', and the control comparison is stated beside it.\nV-S the V-C differences read against the SiLU seed range and the ReLU seed range of rule.txt and rule_relu_seeds.txt, as description.\nLabels per candidate: Gi\u1eef when G1 to G4 pass, Lo\u1ea1i when a step fails (the first failing step is named), Ch\u01b0a bi\u1ebft when the steps did not all run or G1 is partial with A, B, C passing.\nContext recorded before the runs (val mAP50-95 in metrics.csv, descriptive): SiLU 100 epochs 0.4508 at epoch 50, 0.5049 at 80, 0.5223 at 100. ReLU 100 epochs 0.3993, 0.4653, 0.4835. Both still rise between epoch 90 and 100. Ultralytics patience is 100, so a 200 epoch run is expected to run the full 200 unless val mAP does not improve for 100 epochs (the actual number of epochs is read from metrics.csv).\nLatency (A and B) of the variants is a separate interleaved run with its own rule (experiments/npu/operator_support/onboard_g4v/ppe5_yolov8n_baseline_100ep_s0/rule.txt).\nLimit: one seed per candidate, one split of 82 images, ReLU6 and LeakyReLU slope are single points.\nBudget: experiment 1 per candidate.\n",
 "verdict_c": "kh\u00f4ng \u0111\u1ea1t",
 "rule": "G4 C and seed-noise rule (eval_g4), written 2026-10-31T11:37:41+07:00 before any RKNNLite INT8 or FP16 mAP result of baseline seeds 1 and 2 and before any result of ReLU exists (FP32 PyTorch results of seeds 1 and 2 from training already exist, descriptive only). Not from a source. Not reviewed by the user (goal of 2026-10-31, phase 2). The number 1.0 pp (approved 2026-10-25, page 01-operator-support section 2) is the only threshold. Everything else here is new and unreviewed.\nQuestions: G4C (ReLU against SiLU accuracy) and G4N (how large the seed-to-seed spread is, to read the 1.0 pp margin on css_test with 82 images).\nModels and calibration: baseline SiLU seeds 0, 1, 2 (ppe5_yolov8n_baseline_100ep_s{0,1,2}) and ReLU seed 0 (ppe5_yolov8n_relu_100ep_s0). Every INT8 model is built with the calibration list of baseline seed 0 (export_npu.py --calib-from ppe5_yolov8n_baseline_100ep_s0). Identity proof: stems_md5 (md5 of the sorted stems joined by newline) and png_md5 (md5 of the sorted 'name sha256' lines of the PNG files), computed for seed 0 on 2026-10-31 as 11d6a5c69414a6eafd8b98f99724b0b2 and 6652576adb7608ddf8ff326c57851732, equal in seeds 1 and 2, plus the basenames of rknn_int8/dataset.txt equal line by line. The md5 of dataset.txt itself is not a proof, since it holds absolute paths that contain the run id. Baseline seed 1 INT8 therefore replaces its older export (renamed rknn_int8_ownlist, used by X5). The existing seed 0 INT8 export is untouched. FP16 has no calibration.\nMethod: make evaluate RUN=<run> BACKEND=rknn PREC=int8|fp16 BOARD=minhnhat@192.168.137.49 (Evaluation Protocol v1, RKNNLite on the board, same code as X7 and X7b) for css_test (82 images, the gate set, 41 NoHelmet instances) and ppe2286_ext (180 images, descriptive). FP32 PyTorch (make evaluate BACKEND=pt) is run for every run and set that lacks it and is descriptive only. The script refuses to score on a model sha256 mismatch or a missing image.\nStatements (css_test, per dtype INT8 and FP16, and for the AP50-95, AP NoHelmet, AP Vest columns):\nS-N1 spread over seeds 0, 1, 2 of the baseline: minimum, maximum, range = max minus min, in pp. The 1.0 pp margin is labelled 'trong nhi\u1ec5u seed' only when the range of that column is at least 1.0 pp, and 'ngo\u00e0i nhi\u1ec5u seed' only when the range is below 1.0 pp. Three seeds, so no standard deviation is a conclusion, the sample standard deviation (ddof 1) is reported next to it.\nS-C1 gate C for the ReLU candidate (INT8, the conclusion dtype): difference ReLU seed 0 minus SiLU seed 0 in pp for AP50-95, AP NoHelmet and AP Vest. C passes only when all three differences are at least minus 1.0. It fails when any is below minus 1.0. The same differences for FP16 are a reference and do not decide. FP32 differences are descriptive. Every ReLU result carries the label '1 seed'.\nS-C2 whether a ReLU difference lies inside the S-N1 spread of the same column is stated next to S-C1, as description, it does not change S-C1.\nLimit: ReLU is initialised from the SiLU yolov8n.pt weights (ai/models/yolov8n_relu/yolov8n_relu.py), as the SiLU baseline starts from yolov8n.pt. Seeds 1 and 2 of the baseline only measure the training spread of SiLU, the ReLU training spread is unknown (1 seed).\nThe runs happen when no timing measurement runs on the board (one job at a time). Budget: experiment 1 for G4C and G4N. Re-run only if the model on the board differs or the script aborts.\n",
 "rule_relu_seeds": "ReLU seed spread rule (addendum to rule.txt), written 2026-10-31T13:08:11+07:00 before any result of ReLU seeds 1 and 2 exists. Not from a source. Not reviewed by the user. Scope: user approval of 2026-10-31 (option 1: train ReLU seeds 1 and 2 to describe the ReLU seed spread). The 1.0 pp threshold and gate G4 are unchanged: gate C stays ReLU seed 0 against SiLU seed 0, label 'Lo\u1ea1i' is not re-decided here.\nRuns: ppe5_yolov8n_relu_100ep_s1 and _s2 (same config as seed 0, make train SEED=n, init from yolov8n.pt like seed 0). INT8 export with the calibration list of baseline seed 0 (export_npu.py --calib-from, identity md5 as in rule.txt), FP16 export, then the same evaluations as rule.txt (RKNNLite INT8 and FP16 on the board, FP32 PyTorch, css_test and ppe2286_ext).\nStatements (css_test, INT8, FP16, FP32, columns AP50-95, AP NoHelmet, AP Vest, in pp):\nR-1 ReLU spread over seeds 0, 1, 2: minimum, maximum, range, sample standard deviation (ddof 1).\nR-2 mean over three seeds of ReLU minus mean over three seeds of SiLU (SiLU seeds 0, 1, 2 of rule.txt), per column. The difference is 'l\u1edbn h\u01a1n nhi\u1ec5u seed' when its absolute value is larger than the larger of the two ranges (SiLU and ReLU) of that column, otherwise 'trong nhi\u1ec5u seed'. Description only, three seeds do not support a test.\nR-3 whether the seed 0 difference of gate C (ReLU seed 0 minus SiLU seed 0) lies inside the larger of the two ranges, per column. Description only.\nR-4 the number of ReLU seeds (out of 3) whose INT8 css_test passes gate C against the SiLU seed of the same number (seed n against seed n), as description. It does not change the label of gate C.\nLimit: three seeds, one dataset split of 82 images, ReLU initialised from SiLU weights.\nBudget: experiment 1. No re-run unless the script aborts.\n"
}
